  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two beams of light having intensities <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi></math> interfere to produce a fringe pattern on a screen. The phase difference between the two beams are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;at points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> respectively. The difference between the resultant intensities at the two points is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>I</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given here, phase difference at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Resultant intensity at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi></msqrt><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>Resultant intensity at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi></msqrt><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>Difference in intensities is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>I</mi></math>.</p><p>Thus, value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
